<title>UK: Nigeria says it produced at quota in Jan - OPECNA.</title>
<headline>Nigeria says it produced at quota in Jan - OPECNA.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nigeria told OPEC it produced 1.865 million barrels per day (bpd) in January and supplied 1.864 million bpd to the market,the OPEC News Agency OPECNA reported on Thursday.</p>
<p>The West African producer was the latest to report its production numbers for January to the OPEC Secretariat in Vienna. Nigeria has an OPEC quota of 1.865 million bpd.</p>
<p>A Reuters survey of officials, industry monitors and analysts put the country's January wellhead output at 2.10 million bpd.</p>
<p>Supply, as defined by OPEC, is calculated as domestic consumption, plus net export sales of crude and products, plus withdrawals of stocks held outside national boundaries.</p>
<p>Production and supply data for the month of January received by the OPEC Secretariat from member countries is as follows (in thousand bpd):</p>
<p>COUNTRY	  PRODUCTION	SUPPLY     QUOTA</p>
<p>-------	  ----------	------     -----</p>
<p>Algeria	   795.0	     789.0	750.0</p>
<p>Indonesia     1,328.2	   1,326.2    1,330.0</p>
<p>Iran	    3,596.0	   3,596.0    3,600.0</p>
<p>Iraq	    1,340.0	   1,340.0    1,200.0</p>
<p>Kuwait	  2,005.7	   2,005.2    2,000.0</p>
<p>Libya	   1,393.0	   1,394.0    1,390.0</p>
<p>Nigeria	 1,865.0	   1,864.2    1,865.0</p>
<p>Qatar	     399.1	     387.3	378.0</p>
<p>Saudi Arabia  8,005.1	   8,006.1    8,000.0</p>
<p>UAE	     2,226.8	   2,160.5    2,161.0</p>
<p>Venezuela     2,405.0	   2,396.9    2,359.0</p>
